{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AFHdqPjsYEoJGExqueZXjk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario they defined in Phase 1.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n- exception_only ≈ VOTA (gap < 2pp, p > 0.05)\n- loop_only ≈ no_trace, loop compression contributes nothing\n- trivial rule (has_ERROR → fail, else → pass) reaches 90%+ accuracy, close to exception_only\n- VOTA's 99.2% can be simplified to \"error flag + assertion presence detection\"\n\n\n- Claim 3 completely fails, Claim 1's \"genuine behavioral understanding\" needs major revision\n\nNow I'm looking at the metric ranges for this worst-case scenario and seeing how the key measurements would distribute across the experiments. I need to go through each planned experiment and generate specific predictions based on these bounds.\n\nLooking at what's already complete versus what's still ahead: the first three experiments are done with their results, but I still need to work through the ablation studies, the second model comparison, the additional task, trace length effects, calibration analysis, and seed robustness testing.\n\nFor the VOTA component ablation specifically, I'm breaking down what each isolated component contributes under worst-case conditions. The exception detection alone seems to drive most of the performance gains, while loop compression by itself barely helps. The autoencoder component is the tricky one to evaluate in isolation. I'm seeing the experimental setup more clearly now—there are four variants being tested: actual/expected values only, exception summaries only, loop compression only, and the full VOTA approach. Looking at the registry, exception_only is already done but failed, while the others are in various stages. Under the worst-case tier, exception_only hits 0.975 which essentially matches full VOTA performance, loop_only drops to 0.75 matching the no-trace baseline, and ae_only lands around 0.87 with some signal from assertion comparisons but missing the critical error flag information. Now I'm moving to plan_004 to test with DeepSeek-Coder as a second model, expecting the same performance pattern to hold.\n\nThe key insight is that if VOTA's success on this model is really just about extracting error flags, then testing on a different task like bug detection or patch correctness becomes crucial—if error flags aren't as directly informative for that task, VOTA's advantage might disappear, which would actually strengthen the finding that the mechanism is trivial rather than something more sophisticated.\n\nFor the trace length ablation, I'm predicting that under the worst-case scenario, accuracy wouldn't improve with longer traces in the expected way. Instead, performance would depend on whether the truncated trace happens to contain the error signal, so shorter traces that capture the error might perform just as well as longer ones, while traces that miss the error signal would underperform regardless of length.\n\nLooking at calibration, VOTA would show artificially good calibration since it's essentially just flagging errors, whereas the full trace approach would have moderate calibration and no_trace would be poorly calibrated. For seed robustness, I'm checking how consistent VOTA's performance is across different random seeds.\n\nNow I need to construct the YAML output, making sure to include the trivial rule baseline that defines the worst tier ceiling, and then detail the sub-experiments for plan_003 with specific accuracy predictions for the exception-only variant.\n\nFor the ablation studies, exception_only should perform nearly identically to VOTA since the error flag is the critical signal, while loop_only drops significantly without that diagnostic information, and actual/expected values alone provide intermediate performance by capturing some failure indicators through value mismatches.\n\nThe trivial rule based on error flags and assertion structure achieves surprisingly high accuracy by distilling the core decision logic, and the statistical tests confirm these differences aren't significant at the worst tier level—the McNemar tests show exception_only and loop_only are statistically indistinguishable from their respective baselines.\n\nNow I'm reviewing how this pattern holds across the remaining experiment plans: DeepSeek-Coder replicates the same error-flag dependency, the second task shows VOTA succeeding through structural signals rather than semantic understanding, short traces with error information match longer traces, calibration appears artificially strong, and seed robustness is high precisely because the underlying signal is so trivial. Before finalizing the output, I need to clarify what the user meant by \"planned\" experiments—whether they're asking for all experiments with status=planned or something else.\n\nLooking back at the request, I think they want predictions for all incomplete experiments: plan_003 which is partially running, and plans_004 through 008 which are fully planned. Since plan_003 has some conditions already failing or in progress, I should generate predictions for all its sub-conditions to maintain consistency. I also need to ensure the imagined results reinforce the worst-tier narrative and reframe the paper as an empirical decomposition of what makes traces effective for verdict tasks.\n\nNow I'm ready to construct the YAML output with all the necessary experiment details.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13895,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13895},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7c66b2c-1925-497f-a2f7-83e1d0b40d81","uuid":"359f7a3b-83ad-4874-9439-30f79d79f1c6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AFHdqPjsYEoJGExqueZXjk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事崩塌点：exception_only 与 VOTA 无统计显著差异，证明 VOTA 99.2% 的效果本质是\n  error flag extraction 而非 execution-grounded reasoning。loop compression 无贡献\n  （≈ no_trace），ae 信号中等但有 fallback 污染。trivial rule (has_ERROR→fail) 达 93%，\n  逼近 exception_only。论文必须放弃 \"behavioral understanding\" 和 \"component design principles\"，\n  转向 \"What Makes Traces Work for Verdict Tasks? An Empirical Decomposition\"。\n  Claim 3 完全失败（无 component hierarchy），Claim 1 大幅削弱（genuine→signal extraction），\n  Claim 2 不受影响。EMNLP Main 概率降至 ~30%，Findings 仍 solid。\n  关键防线：full_trace 也有 ERROR 信号但仅 81.8%，说明 information overload 仍是真实现象——\n  但 \"解药\" 不是 intelligent compression 而只是 isolate the error flag。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: VOTA component ablation — 核心 worst-tier 实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 exception summary 组件（[ERROR] Traceback... / [No exceptions]），\n      去除 assertion snapshots 和 loop compression。训练数据中 trace 字段仅含异常摘要。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.980\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.970\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.989\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.229\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: 0.205\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.253\n      pass_f1: 0.987\n      fail_f1: 0.960\n      train_loss: 0.095\n      eval_loss: 0.180\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.012\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.25\n      mcnemar_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，exception summary 包含了 VOTA 几乎全部的 decision-relevant signal：\n      [ERROR] 标记直接映射 fail，[No exceptions] 高度相关 pass。模型只需学会\n      \"有 ERROR → fail, 无 ERROR → pass\" 这一近乎 trivial 的映射。与 VOTA 的差距\n      仅 ~1.2pp（14 样本/1190），McNemar p=0.18 不显著——统计上无法拒绝\n      \"exception_only = VOTA\" 的零假设。这证明 assertion snapshots 和 loop compression\n      对 verdict 预测几乎无边际贡献，VOTA 的效果可归约为 error flag extraction。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Component Ablation Accuracy Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA (full)\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+24.0pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"+1.2pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.980\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+22.9pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n          - condition: \"ae_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.875\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+12.4pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-10.5pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n          - condition: \"loop_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.755\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+0.4pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-22.5pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"—\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-22.9pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 条件 accuracy 对比，exception_only 与 VOTA 柱高几乎相同，两者之间标注 n.s.（not significant）；loop_only 与 no_trace 柱高几乎相同。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档的核心打击：exception_only ≈ VOTA 直接摧毁 Claim 3 的 \"component\n      importance hierarchy\"。无法声称各组件有差异化贡献，因为一个组件就解释了\n      几乎全部效果。论文必须将此报告为 negative result：\n      \"We find no evidence that assertion snapshots or loop compression contribute\n      meaningfully beyond what exception summaries alone provide.\"\n      但可以 reframe：这揭示了 verdict tasks 的信息结构——pass/fail 决策的\n      information bottleneck 就在 exception presence，这本身是有价值的发现。\n\n  - name: \"loop_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 loop compression 组件（迭代次数、收敛摘要），\n      去除 exception summary 和 assertion snapshots。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.755\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.730\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.778\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.004\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: -0.025\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.033\n      lift_vs_notrace_pvalue: 0.72\n      pass_f1: 0.820\n      fail_f1: 0.635\n      train_loss: 0.175\n      eval_loss: 0.610\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      Loop compression 记录的是循环执行模式（迭代次数、early termination），\n      这些信息与 pass/fail verdict 的相关性极弱。在 worst 档下，\n      测试通过/失败几乎完全由异常有无决定，循环行为是 verdict-orthogonal\n      的执行细节。loop_only 的信息价值 ≈ 随机噪声，模型退化到与 no_trace\n      相同的 majority-leaning 行为。lift 仅 +0.4pp，CI 跨零，p=0.72。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      loop_only ≈ no_trace 证实 loop compression 对 verdict task 无贡献。\n      这进一步支持 worst 档叙事：VOTA 的全部效果来自 exception signal，\n      loop 和 assertion 是 dead weight。但需注意：这不能证明 loop\n      compression 对所有任务无用——它可能对 generation tasks 有价值。\n\n  - name: \"ae_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 actual/expected 值对（assertion point 的具体数值），\n      去除 exception summary 和 loop compression。已知有 fallback 污染问题。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.875\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.853\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.896\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.124\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: 0.098\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.150\n      pass_f1: 0.910\n      fail_f1: 0.790\n      train_loss: 0.140\n      eval_loss: 0.350\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      ae_only 包含 actual vs expected 数值，mismatch 间接暗示 failure，但信号远不如\n      ERROR flag 直接。且存在 fallback 污染：部分样本因 trace 生成失败使用了\n      fallback template，引入了 systematic bias。在 worst 档下 ae_only 比 no_trace\n      好 12.4pp（数值比对有一定诊断价值），但远不及 exception_only 的 22.9pp，\n      且受 fallback 污染无法做可靠归因。此结果移至 Appendix 附 caveat。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      ae_only 的中等表现 (87.5%) 看似为 ae 组件提供了存在价值，但 plan_001\n      已证明去除 ae 后 VOTA 不降反升 (99.4%)，说明 ae 信息是 redundant 而非\n      complementary。ae_only 的 87.5% 更可能来自 actual/expected mismatch 作为\n      error 的 noisy proxy，而非独立的推理通道。Fallback 污染使此结论进一步弱化。\n\n  - name: \"trivial_rule_baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      无需训练的 rule-based baseline：检查 trace 文本中是否包含 ERROR/Exception\n      关键词 → fail；包含 ASSERT 且无 ERROR → pass；无 trace → majority vote。\n      纯 eval 实验，直接在测试集上计算。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.930\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.912\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.946\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.179\n      pass_f1: 0.952\n      fail_f1: 0.872\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.050\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.062\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，test verdict 的 ground truth 与 ERROR presence 高度相关。\n      trivial rule 不需要 SFT，不需要理解 trace 语义，仅做关键词匹配就达到 93%。\n      这意味着 exception_only SFT 的 98% 中约 93pp 可被 trivial rule 解释，\n      SFT 的真正边际贡献仅 ~5pp（处理 error 信息缺失或 ambiguous 的边缘情况）。\n      这是对 \"behavioral understanding\" framing 的致命打击：reviewer 可以合理质疑\n      \"你训了个 7B 模型做关键词匹配？\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Trivial Rule vs SFT Conditions\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 2\n          - condition: \"exception_only SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.980\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 2\n          - condition: \"trivial_rule (no training)\"\n            accuracy: 0.930\n            requires_training: false\n            gpu_hours: 0\n          - condition: \"no_trace SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 1\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar 或 waterfall chart：从 no_trace (75.1%) → trivial_rule (93.0%) → exception_only (98.0%) → VOTA (99.2%)，标注每段增益来源。trivial_rule→exception_only 的 5pp 标注为 'SFT marginal gain over keyword matching'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      trivial rule 93% 是 worst 档最 damaging 的数字之一。它证明 VOTA trace 中的\n      \"information\" 大部分可被无参数规则捕获。SFT 的额外 5-6pp 可能来自：\n      (1) 处理 ERROR 信号缺失但实际 fail 的边缘案例，\n      (2) 处理有 ERROR 但实际 pass 的 flaky test，\n      (3) 更好的 no_trace 样本处理。\n      论文需要在 Discussion 中诚实面对这个数字，但可以辩护：\n      \"The fact that a trivial rule achieves 93% confirms our decomposition finding\n      that error status is the dominant signal. SFT's value is in handling the\n      remaining 7% where the signal is ambiguous — precisely the cases where\n      genuine reasoning about execution state is needed.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: 第二模型验证 (DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_vota\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 VOTA condition，与 DCSH 同模型直接对比。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.978\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.966\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.988\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.222\n      pass_f1: 0.985\n      fail_f1: 0.955\n      train_loss: 0.100\n      eval_loss: 0.195\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder 代码理解能力略弱于主实验模型，VOTA 准确率可能略低 (~97.8% vs 99.2%)\n      但仍远超 baseline。在 worst 档下，这反而加强负面叙事：即使换模型，\n      error flag extraction 仍然足以达到 ~98%，说明高准确率不是模型特异的\n      \"理解能力\" 而是 task-data 结构决定的 trivial pattern。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_notrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 no_trace baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.756\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.731\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.780\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift: 0.041\n      pass_f1: 0.822\n      fail_f1: 0.635\n      train_loss: 0.185\n      eval_loss: 0.640\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      No-trace baseline 不依赖 trace 信息，主要靠代码 pattern 和 test 名推断结果。\n      DeepSeek-Coder 与主模型在 no_trace 上差异极小（75.6% vs 75.1%），\n      因为两者的 code understanding 在不看 trace 时差异有限。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_fulltrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 full_trace condition。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.805\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.782\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.828\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.049\n      pass_f1: 0.862\n      fail_f1: 0.670\n      train_loss: 0.055\n      eval_loss: 0.095\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder 在 full_trace 上预期略低于主模型 (80.5% vs 81.8%)，\n      因为较弱的模型在 information overload 场景下更容易被 irrelevant trace detail\n      干扰。full_trace 包含 ERROR 信号但被大量无关执行细节淹没，\n      模型难以稳定提取 decision signal。三条件层次 (no_trace < full_trace < VOTA)\n      在第二模型上复现，但在 worst 档下这只是说明 error flag 的 surface-level\n      accessibility 差异，不是 reasoning depth 差异。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      追加实验：如果主实验已确认 exception_only ≈ VOTA，\n      在 DeepSeek-Coder 上验证此等价性是否跨模型成立。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.972\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.984\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.006\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.45\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      如果 exception_only ≈ VOTA 是 task structure 决定的而非模型特异的，\n      那么在 DeepSeek-Coder 上也应成立。worst 档预测 gap 仅 0.6pp，p=0.45，\n      跨模型一致证实 error flag extraction 假说。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Model Replication (3+1 conditions)\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"CodeLlama-7B (primary)\"\n            no_trace: 0.751\n            full_trace: 0.818\n            vota: 0.992\n            exception_only: 0.980\n          - model: \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B\"\n            no_trace: 0.756\n            full_trace: 0.805\n            vota: 0.978\n            exception_only: 0.972\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 两模型 × 四条件，展示 pattern 跨模型一致性。标注 exception_only 与 VOTA 在两模型上均为 n.s.。\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨模型复现在 worst 档下是双刃剑：证明了结果的 robustness（reviewer 喜欢），\n      但也证明了 error flag extraction 的 trivialness 是 task-structural 而非\n      model-dependent（加强负面解读）。论文应如实报告，在 Discussion 中转化为：\n      \"The cross-model consistency of exception-only equivalence confirms that\n      verdict prediction effectiveness is driven by task information structure,\n      not model-specific reasoning capabilities — a finding that directly informs\n      trace design for future verdict-oriented SFT.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: 第二任务验证 (DebugBench / Patch Correctness)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"second_task_vota\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      在 DebugBench (Python subset) 的 bug detection verdict task 上测试 VOTA。\n      任务：给定代码+测试+VOTA trace，预测是否有 bug（binary verdict）。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.885\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.860\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.908\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.195\n      pass_f1: 0.890\n      fail_f1: 0.878\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      DebugBench 的 bug detection 与 test verdict 的关键区别：buggy 代码不一定\n      产生 runtime ERROR（可能是 logic bug 导致 wrong output），因此 error flag\n      不再是完美的 decision signal。在 worst 档下，VOTA 仍然有效 (+19.5pp)\n      但准确率显著低于 test verdict 的 99.2%，因为 bug detection 需要的\n      信号更复杂（值比对、逻辑推理），不能被 trivial error flag extraction 覆盖。\n      讽刺的是，这反而部分挽救了论文——证明 test verdict task 的 near-perfect\n      性能确实有 task-specific 原因（error signal dominance），而不同 verdict tasks\n      需要不同的 trace 设计。\n\n  - name: \"second_task_notrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      DebugBench no_trace baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.690\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.658\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.722\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift: 0.170\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bug detection 的 no_trace baseline 高于 test verdict (69% vs 75.1%) 的\n      绝对值可能不同，但 lift over majority 更大 (+17pp vs +3.6pp)，\n      因为 DebugBench 的 majority baseline 更低 (52% vs 71.5%)。\n\n  - name: \"second_task_exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      DebugBench exception_only condition。验证 error flag extraction 在第二任务上\n      是否仍是 dominant mechanism。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.815\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.787\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.842\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.125\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.070\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.001\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 DebugBench 上 exception_only ≠ VOTA（gap 7pp, p<0.01），因为 logic bugs\n      不触发 exception，exception_only 错失这部分信号。这与 test verdict task 上\n      exception_only ≈ VOTA 形成对比，支持更细致的结论：error flag extraction\n      是 test verdict 的 dominant mechanism 但不是所有 verdict tasks 的。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Task Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - task: \"Test Verdict\"\n            no_trace: 0.751\n            exception_only: 0.980\n            vota: 0.992\n            exception_only_vs_vota_gap: \"-1.2pp (n.s.)\"\n          - task: \"Bug Detection (DebugBench)\"\n            no_trace: 0.690\n            exception_only: 0.815\n            vota: 0.885\n            exception_only_vs_vota_gap: \"-7.0pp (p<0.01)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side grouped bars: 两任务 × 三条件。关键视觉信息：test verdict 上 exception_only ≈ VOTA（平齐），bug detection 上 exception_only < VOTA（明显落差）。标注 significance levels。\"\n    analysis: >\n      第二任务结果在 worst 档下产生有趣的 tension：test verdict 的 exception_only ≈ VOTA\n      证实了 error flag extraction 假说，但 bug detection 的 exception_only < VOTA\n      说明 VOTA 的其他组件在非 error-dominated 任务上确实有贡献。这为论文提供了\n      nuanced narrative：\"The dominance of error signals is task-dependent.\n      For verdict tasks where failures manifest as runtime exceptions (test outcomes),\n      error flag extraction suffices. For verdict tasks involving logic errors\n      (bug detection), richer trace components become necessary.\"\n      这个 task-dependent finding 可能比原始的 \"universal design principles\" 更有\n      intellectual depth，但也更复杂、更难在一篇论文中充分论证。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Trace length ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"trace_length_256\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 256 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.862\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.838\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.884\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      256 tokens 通常足以包含 ERROR traceback 的前几行（如果在 trace 开头或结尾出现）。\n      在 worst 档下，短 trace 只要捕获 error flag 就足够。但 256 tokens 有时会\n      截断到 trace 中间的无关执行步骤，错失 ERROR 信号。准确率接近 label-only\n      full_trace (86.2%)，因为两者都是 \"partial error signal access\"。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_512\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 512 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.845\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.821\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.868\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      512 tokens 捕获更多 trace context 但也引入更多 noise。在 worst 档下，\n      当 trace 中 ERROR 出现在较后位置时 512 能捕获但 256 不能，\n      但额外 noise 部分抵消了信息增益。准确率与 256 差异不大。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_1024\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 1024 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.830\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.806\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.854\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      1024 tokens 几乎总能包含 ERROR 信号（如果存在），但同时大量无关执行细节\n      开始显著稀释 signal density。在 worst 档下出现反直觉现象：\n      更长 trace 准确率反而略低，因为 noise-to-signal ratio 恶化。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_2048\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 2048 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.820\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.795\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.843\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      接近 full_trace (81.8%) 的水平，因为大部分 trace 在 2048 tokens 内。\n      标准训练的 full_trace 用 standard loss 是 81.8%，但此处用 standard loss\n      所以结果基本一致。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Accuracy vs Trace Length\"\n        rows:\n          - length: \"VOTA (~80 tokens avg)\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            tokens_per_sample: 80\n          - length: \"256 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.862\n            tokens_per_sample: 256\n          - length: \"512 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.845\n            tokens_per_sample: 512\n          - length: \"1024 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.830\n            tokens_per_sample: 1024\n          - length: \"2048 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.820\n            tokens_per_sample: 2048\n          - length: \"Full trace (avg ~3200)\"\n            accuracy: 0.818\n            tokens_per_sample: 3200\n          - length: \"No trace\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            tokens_per_sample: 0\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Line plot: X 轴 = trace tokens (log scale: 0, 80, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 3200),\n        Y 轴 = accuracy。关键视觉特征：(1) VOTA 在 80 tokens 处达到最高点 99.2%，\n        与主曲线脱离（单独标注为 ★）；(2) 截断 trace 从 256→3200 呈微弱下降趋势\n        （86.2% → 81.8%），而非预期的上升；(3) no_trace 在 0 处为 75.1%。\n        标注：\"More trace ≠ better prediction — signal density dominates.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace length ablation 在 worst 档下产生 \"inverted U\" 或近似 monotonic decline：\n      短 trace 比长 trace 好（因为 error signal 的 density 更高），但都远不及 VOTA\n      （因为 VOTA 直接 isolate 了 signal）。这支持 \"information overload\" 叙事，\n      但在 worst 档解读下，\"overload\" 的本质不是 \"execution detail 干扰 reasoning\"\n      而是 \"keyword dilution 降低 pattern matching accuracy\"。\n      此图表在论文中仍有高价值——它直观展示了 signal density 假说，\n      只是 underlying mechanism 比原 framing 更 trivial。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Calibration analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"calibration_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      ECE (Expected Calibration Error) + reliability diagrams 对比\n      VOTA/no_trace/full_trace 的 calibration 质量。纯 eval 实验。\n    expected_results:\n      vota_ece: 0.008\n      vota_brier: 0.012\n      exception_only_ece: 0.015\n      exception_only_brier: 0.022\n      full_trace_ece: 0.085\n      full_trace_brier: 0.145\n      full_trace_label_only_ece: 0.068\n      full_trace_label_only_brier: 0.115\n      no_trace_ece: 0.165\n      no_trace_brier: 0.225\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，VOTA 和 exception_only 都有极低的 ECE，因为它们本质上是\n      near-deterministic 的 pattern matching（看到 ERROR → 高置信度 fail）。\n      calibration 好不是因为 \"深层理解产生了 well-calibrated uncertainty\"，\n      而是因为 signal 太强导致模型几乎不产生 uncertain predictions。\n      full_trace 的 ECE 较高反映了 noise-induced uncertainty，\n      no_trace 最高因为缺少 decision signal 导致系统性 miscalibration。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Calibration Metrics\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA\"\n            ece: 0.008\n            brier: 0.012\n            mean_confidence: 0.985\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            ece: 0.015\n            brier: 0.022\n            mean_confidence: 0.975\n          - condition: \"full_trace_label_only\"\n            ece: 0.068\n            brier: 0.115\n            mean_confidence: 0.890\n          - condition: \"full_trace\"\n            ece: 0.085\n            brier: 0.145\n            mean_confidence: 0.870\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            ece: 0.165\n            brier: 0.225\n            mean_confidence: 0.780\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        5-panel reliability diagram (one per condition)：X 轴 = predicted probability,\n        Y 轴 = observed frequency, 对角线 = perfect calibration。\n        VOTA 和 exception_only 的点集中在 (0,0) 和 (1,1) 两端（near-binary predictions），\n        几乎不在中间；no_trace 的点散布更广且偏离对角线。\n      - >\n        Single-panel ECE bar chart: 5 条件从低到高排列，VOTA/exception_only 几乎为零，\n        no_trace 最高。\n    analysis: >\n      Calibration 结果在 worst 档下的论文价值有限：VOTA 的 excellent calibration\n      是 near-perfect accuracy 的 trivial 后果，不提供额外 insight。\n      但 full_trace 的 poor calibration 可以用来支持 \"information overload causes\n      not just accuracy drop but also uncertainty increase\" 的叙事点。\n      建议放 Appendix 而非主文，避免 reviewer 指出 \"of course a 99% accurate\n      model is well-calibrated\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Seed robustness\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"seed_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      3 random seeds (42/123/456) 验证 VOTA 结果稳定性。McNemar test + bootstrap CI。\n    expected_results:\n      seed_42_accuracy: 0.992\n      seed_123_accuracy: 0.988\n      seed_456_accuracy: 0.990\n      mean_accuracy: 0.990\n      std_accuracy: 0.002\n      max_pairwise_gap: 0.004\n      mcnemar_max_pvalue: 0.55\n      bootstrap_ci_lower: 0.985\n      bootstrap_ci_upper: 0.995\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，VOTA 跨 seed 极其稳定（std < 0.2pp），因为 error flag signal\n      太强，training randomness 几乎不影响 learned decision boundary。任何 seed\n      都能在 early training 阶段学会 ERROR→fail 映射。高稳定性在论文中是正面结果\n      但在 worst 档叙事下也是 trivialness 的又一证据：真正困难的 task 不会有\n      0.2pp 的跨 seed 方差。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Seed Robustness (VOTA)\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: 42\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            pass_f1: 0.994\n            fail_f1: 0.986\n          - seed: 123\n            accuracy: 0.988\n            pass_f1: 0.992\n            fail_f1: 0.979\n          - seed: 456\n            accuracy: 0.990\n            pass_f1: 0.993\n            fail_f1: 0.982\n          - seed: \"Mean ± Std\"\n            accuracy: \"0.990 ± 0.002\"\n            pass_f1: \"0.993 ± 0.001\"\n            fail_f1: \"0.982 ± 0.004\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error bar plot: 3 seeds 的 accuracy ± CI，紧密聚集在 99% 附近。标注 'All pairwise McNemar p > 0.5'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Seed robustness 在所有 tiers 下都是正面的（结果稳定），区别在于解读。\n      在 worst 档下，需在 Discussion 中承认：\"The low variance across seeds\n      is consistent with our finding that the learned decision function is\n      dominated by a strong surface-level signal (error presence), which is\n      easily captured regardless of initialization.\" 但不需要 apologize——\n      robustness is robustness，reviewer 不会因为结果太稳定而 reject。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13895,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13895},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7c66b2c-1925-497f-a2f7-83e1d0b40d81","uuid":"d2274cf7-3b03-44e3-b37e-dd8f90df4d6a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":249458,"duration_api_ms":250836,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事崩塌点：exception_only 与 VOTA 无统计显著差异，证明 VOTA 99.2% 的效果本质是\n  error flag extraction 而非 execution-grounded reasoning。loop compression 无贡献\n  （≈ no_trace），ae 信号中等但有 fallback 污染。trivial rule (has_ERROR→fail) 达 93%，\n  逼近 exception_only。论文必须放弃 \"behavioral understanding\" 和 \"component design principles\"，\n  转向 \"What Makes Traces Work for Verdict Tasks? An Empirical Decomposition\"。\n  Claim 3 完全失败（无 component hierarchy），Claim 1 大幅削弱（genuine→signal extraction），\n  Claim 2 不受影响。EMNLP Main 概率降至 ~30%，Findings 仍 solid。\n  关键防线：full_trace 也有 ERROR 信号但仅 81.8%，说明 information overload 仍是真实现象——\n  但 \"解药\" 不是 intelligent compression 而只是 isolate the error flag。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: VOTA component ablation — 核心 worst-tier 实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 exception summary 组件（[ERROR] Traceback... / [No exceptions]），\n      去除 assertion snapshots 和 loop compression。训练数据中 trace 字段仅含异常摘要。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.980\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.970\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.989\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.229\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: 0.205\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.253\n      pass_f1: 0.987\n      fail_f1: 0.960\n      train_loss: 0.095\n      eval_loss: 0.180\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.012\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.25\n      mcnemar_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，exception summary 包含了 VOTA 几乎全部的 decision-relevant signal：\n      [ERROR] 标记直接映射 fail，[No exceptions] 高度相关 pass。模型只需学会\n      \"有 ERROR → fail, 无 ERROR → pass\" 这一近乎 trivial 的映射。与 VOTA 的差距\n      仅 ~1.2pp（14 样本/1190），McNemar p=0.18 不显著——统计上无法拒绝\n      \"exception_only = VOTA\" 的零假设。这证明 assertion snapshots 和 loop compression\n      对 verdict 预测几乎无边际贡献，VOTA 的效果可归约为 error flag extraction。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Component Ablation Accuracy Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA (full)\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+24.0pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"+1.2pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.980\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+22.9pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"—\"\n          - condition: \"ae_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.875\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+12.4pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-10.5pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n          - condition: \"loop_only\"\n            accuracy: 0.755\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"+0.4pp\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-22.5pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            delta_vs_notrace: \"—\"\n            delta_vs_exception_only: \"-22.9pp\"\n            p_vs_exception_only: \"<0.001\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 条件 accuracy 对比，exception_only 与 VOTA 柱高几乎相同，两者之间标注 n.s.（not significant）；loop_only 与 no_trace 柱高几乎相同。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档的核心打击：exception_only ≈ VOTA 直接摧毁 Claim 3 的 \"component\n      importance hierarchy\"。无法声称各组件有差异化贡献，因为一个组件就解释了\n      几乎全部效果。论文必须将此报告为 negative result：\n      \"We find no evidence that assertion snapshots or loop compression contribute\n      meaningfully beyond what exception summaries alone provide.\"\n      但可以 reframe：这揭示了 verdict tasks 的信息结构——pass/fail 决策的\n      information bottleneck 就在 exception presence，这本身是有价值的发现。\n\n  - name: \"loop_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 loop compression 组件（迭代次数、收敛摘要），\n      去除 exception summary 和 assertion snapshots。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.755\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.730\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.778\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.004\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: -0.025\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.033\n      lift_vs_notrace_pvalue: 0.72\n      pass_f1: 0.820\n      fail_f1: 0.635\n      train_loss: 0.175\n      eval_loss: 0.610\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      Loop compression 记录的是循环执行模式（迭代次数、early termination），\n      这些信息与 pass/fail verdict 的相关性极弱。在 worst 档下，\n      测试通过/失败几乎完全由异常有无决定，循环行为是 verdict-orthogonal\n      的执行细节。loop_only 的信息价值 ≈ 随机噪声，模型退化到与 no_trace\n      相同的 majority-leaning 行为。lift 仅 +0.4pp，CI 跨零，p=0.72。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      loop_only ≈ no_trace 证实 loop compression 对 verdict task 无贡献。\n      这进一步支持 worst 档叙事：VOTA 的全部效果来自 exception signal，\n      loop 和 assertion 是 dead weight。但需注意：这不能证明 loop\n      compression 对所有任务无用——它可能对 generation tasks 有价值。\n\n  - name: \"ae_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      只保留 VOTA 中的 actual/expected 值对（assertion point 的具体数值），\n      去除 exception summary 和 loop compression。已知有 fallback 污染问题。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.875\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.853\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.896\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.124\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_lower: 0.098\n      lift_vs_notrace_ci_upper: 0.150\n      pass_f1: 0.910\n      fail_f1: 0.790\n      train_loss: 0.140\n      eval_loss: 0.350\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      ae_only 包含 actual vs expected 数值，mismatch 间接暗示 failure，但信号远不如\n      ERROR flag 直接。且存在 fallback 污染：部分样本因 trace 生成失败使用了\n      fallback template，引入了 systematic bias。在 worst 档下 ae_only 比 no_trace\n      好 12.4pp（数值比对有一定诊断价值），但远不及 exception_only 的 22.9pp，\n      且受 fallback 污染无法做可靠归因。此结果移至 Appendix 附 caveat。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      ae_only 的中等表现 (87.5%) 看似为 ae 组件提供了存在价值，但 plan_001\n      已证明去除 ae 后 VOTA 不降反升 (99.4%)，说明 ae 信息是 redundant 而非\n      complementary。ae_only 的 87.5% 更可能来自 actual/expected mismatch 作为\n      error 的 noisy proxy，而非独立的推理通道。Fallback 污染使此结论进一步弱化。\n\n  - name: \"trivial_rule_baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      无需训练的 rule-based baseline：检查 trace 文本中是否包含 ERROR/Exception\n      关键词 → fail；包含 ASSERT 且无 ERROR → pass；无 trace → majority vote。\n      纯 eval 实验，直接在测试集上计算。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.930\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.912\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.946\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.179\n      pass_f1: 0.952\n      fail_f1: 0.872\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.050\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.062\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，test verdict 的 ground truth 与 ERROR presence 高度相关。\n      trivial rule 不需要 SFT，不需要理解 trace 语义，仅做关键词匹配就达到 93%。\n      这意味着 exception_only SFT 的 98% 中约 93pp 可被 trivial rule 解释，\n      SFT 的真正边际贡献仅 ~5pp（处理 error 信息缺失或 ambiguous 的边缘情况）。\n      这是对 \"behavioral understanding\" framing 的致命打击：reviewer 可以合理质疑\n      \"你训了个 7B 模型做关键词匹配？\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Trivial Rule vs SFT Conditions\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 2\n          - condition: \"exception_only SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.980\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 2\n          - condition: \"trivial_rule (no training)\"\n            accuracy: 0.930\n            requires_training: false\n            gpu_hours: 0\n          - condition: \"no_trace SFT\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            requires_training: true\n            gpu_hours: 1\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar 或 waterfall chart：从 no_trace (75.1%) → trivial_rule (93.0%) → exception_only (98.0%) → VOTA (99.2%)，标注每段增益来源。trivial_rule→exception_only 的 5pp 标注为 'SFT marginal gain over keyword matching'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      trivial rule 93% 是 worst 档最 damaging 的数字之一。它证明 VOTA trace 中的\n      \"information\" 大部分可被无参数规则捕获。SFT 的额外 5-6pp 可能来自：\n      (1) 处理 ERROR 信号缺失但实际 fail 的边缘案例，\n      (2) 处理有 ERROR 但实际 pass 的 flaky test，\n      (3) 更好的 no_trace 样本处理。\n      论文需要在 Discussion 中诚实面对这个数字，但可以辩护：\n      \"The fact that a trivial rule achieves 93% confirms our decomposition finding\n      that error status is the dominant signal. SFT's value is in handling the\n      remaining 7% where the signal is ambiguous — precisely the cases where\n      genuine reasoning about execution state is needed.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: 第二模型验证 (DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_vota\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 VOTA condition，与 DCSH 同模型直接对比。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.978\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.966\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.988\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.222\n      pass_f1: 0.985\n      fail_f1: 0.955\n      train_loss: 0.100\n      eval_loss: 0.195\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder 代码理解能力略弱于主实验模型，VOTA 准确率可能略低 (~97.8% vs 99.2%)\n      但仍远超 baseline。在 worst 档下，这反而加强负面叙事：即使换模型，\n      error flag extraction 仍然足以达到 ~98%，说明高准确率不是模型特异的\n      \"理解能力\" 而是 task-data 结构决定的 trivial pattern。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_notrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 no_trace baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.756\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.731\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.780\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift: 0.041\n      pass_f1: 0.822\n      fail_f1: 0.635\n      train_loss: 0.185\n      eval_loss: 0.640\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      No-trace baseline 不依赖 trace 信息，主要靠代码 pattern 和 test 名推断结果。\n      DeepSeek-Coder 与主模型在 no_trace 上差异极小（75.6% vs 75.1%），\n      因为两者的 code understanding 在不看 trace 时差异有限。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_fulltrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上复现 full_trace condition。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.805\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.782\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.828\n      majority_baseline: 0.7151\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.049\n      pass_f1: 0.862\n      fail_f1: 0.670\n      train_loss: 0.055\n      eval_loss: 0.095\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      DeepSeek-Coder 在 full_trace 上预期略低于主模型 (80.5% vs 81.8%)，\n      因为较弱的模型在 information overload 场景下更容易被 irrelevant trace detail\n      干扰。full_trace 包含 ERROR 信号但被大量无关执行细节淹没，\n      模型难以稳定提取 decision signal。三条件层次 (no_trace < full_trace < VOTA)\n      在第二模型上复现，但在 worst 档下这只是说明 error flag 的 surface-level\n      accessibility 差异，不是 reasoning depth 差异。\n\n  - name: \"deepseek_coder_exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      追加实验：如果主实验已确认 exception_only ≈ VOTA，\n      在 DeepSeek-Coder 上验证此等价性是否跨模型成立。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.972\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.984\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.006\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.45\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      如果 exception_only ≈ VOTA 是 task structure 决定的而非模型特异的，\n      那么在 DeepSeek-Coder 上也应成立。worst 档预测 gap 仅 0.6pp，p=0.45，\n      跨模型一致证实 error flag extraction 假说。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Model Replication (3+1 conditions)\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"CodeLlama-7B (primary)\"\n            no_trace: 0.751\n            full_trace: 0.818\n            vota: 0.992\n            exception_only: 0.980\n          - model: \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B\"\n            no_trace: 0.756\n            full_trace: 0.805\n            vota: 0.978\n            exception_only: 0.972\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 两模型 × 四条件，展示 pattern 跨模型一致性。标注 exception_only 与 VOTA 在两模型上均为 n.s.。\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨模型复现在 worst 档下是双刃剑：证明了结果的 robustness（reviewer 喜欢），\n      但也证明了 error flag extraction 的 trivialness 是 task-structural 而非\n      model-dependent（加强负面解读）。论文应如实报告，在 Discussion 中转化为：\n      \"The cross-model consistency of exception-only equivalence confirms that\n      verdict prediction effectiveness is driven by task information structure,\n      not model-specific reasoning capabilities — a finding that directly informs\n      trace design for future verdict-oriented SFT.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: 第二任务验证 (DebugBench / Patch Correctness)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"second_task_vota\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      在 DebugBench (Python subset) 的 bug detection verdict task 上测试 VOTA。\n      任务：给定代码+测试+VOTA trace，预测是否有 bug（binary verdict）。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.885\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.860\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.908\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.195\n      pass_f1: 0.890\n      fail_f1: 0.878\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      DebugBench 的 bug detection 与 test verdict 的关键区别：buggy 代码不一定\n      产生 runtime ERROR（可能是 logic bug 导致 wrong output），因此 error flag\n      不再是完美的 decision signal。在 worst 档下，VOTA 仍然有效 (+19.5pp)\n      但准确率显著低于 test verdict 的 99.2%，因为 bug detection 需要的\n      信号更复杂（值比对、逻辑推理），不能被 trivial error flag extraction 覆盖。\n      讽刺的是，这反而部分挽救了论文——证明 test verdict task 的 near-perfect\n      性能确实有 task-specific 原因（error signal dominance），而不同 verdict tasks\n      需要不同的 trace 设计。\n\n  - name: \"second_task_notrace\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      DebugBench no_trace baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.690\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.658\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.722\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift: 0.170\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bug detection 的 no_trace baseline 高于 test verdict (69% vs 75.1%) 的\n      绝对值可能不同，但 lift over majority 更大 (+17pp vs +3.6pp)，\n      因为 DebugBench 的 majority baseline 更低 (52% vs 71.5%)。\n\n  - name: \"second_task_exception_only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      DebugBench exception_only condition。验证 error flag extraction 在第二任务上\n      是否仍是 dominant mechanism。\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.815\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.787\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.842\n      majority_baseline: 0.520\n      lift_vs_notrace: 0.125\n      gap_vs_vota: -0.070\n      gap_vs_vota_pvalue: 0.001\n      n: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 DebugBench 上 exception_only ≠ VOTA（gap 7pp, p<0.01），因为 logic bugs\n      不触发 exception，exception_only 错失这部分信号。这与 test verdict task 上\n      exception_only ≈ VOTA 形成对比，支持更细致的结论：error flag extraction\n      是 test verdict 的 dominant mechanism 但不是所有 verdict tasks 的。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Task Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - task: \"Test Verdict\"\n            no_trace: 0.751\n            exception_only: 0.980\n            vota: 0.992\n            exception_only_vs_vota_gap: \"-1.2pp (n.s.)\"\n          - task: \"Bug Detection (DebugBench)\"\n            no_trace: 0.690\n            exception_only: 0.815\n            vota: 0.885\n            exception_only_vs_vota_gap: \"-7.0pp (p<0.01)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side grouped bars: 两任务 × 三条件。关键视觉信息：test verdict 上 exception_only ≈ VOTA（平齐），bug detection 上 exception_only < VOTA（明显落差）。标注 significance levels。\"\n    analysis: >\n      第二任务结果在 worst 档下产生有趣的 tension：test verdict 的 exception_only ≈ VOTA\n      证实了 error flag extraction 假说，但 bug detection 的 exception_only < VOTA\n      说明 VOTA 的其他组件在非 error-dominated 任务上确实有贡献。这为论文提供了\n      nuanced narrative：\"The dominance of error signals is task-dependent.\n      For verdict tasks where failures manifest as runtime exceptions (test outcomes),\n      error flag extraction suffices. For verdict tasks involving logic errors\n      (bug detection), richer trace components become necessary.\"\n      这个 task-dependent finding 可能比原始的 \"universal design principles\" 更有\n      intellectual depth，但也更复杂、更难在一篇论文中充分论证。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Trace length ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"trace_length_256\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 256 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.862\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.838\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.884\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      256 tokens 通常足以包含 ERROR traceback 的前几行（如果在 trace 开头或结尾出现）。\n      在 worst 档下，短 trace 只要捕获 error flag 就足够。但 256 tokens 有时会\n      截断到 trace 中间的无关执行步骤，错失 ERROR 信号。准确率接近 label-only\n      full_trace (86.2%)，因为两者都是 \"partial error signal access\"。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_512\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 512 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.845\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.821\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.868\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      512 tokens 捕获更多 trace context 但也引入更多 noise。在 worst 档下，\n      当 trace 中 ERROR 出现在较后位置时 512 能捕获但 256 不能，\n      但额外 noise 部分抵消了信息增益。准确率与 256 差异不大。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_1024\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 1024 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.830\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.806\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.854\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      1024 tokens 几乎总能包含 ERROR 信号（如果存在），但同时大量无关执行细节\n      开始显著稀释 signal density。在 worst 档下出现反直觉现象：\n      更长 trace 准确率反而略低，因为 noise-to-signal ratio 恶化。\n\n  - name: \"trace_length_2048\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Full trace 截断至 2048 tokens。\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.820\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.795\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.843\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      接近 full_trace (81.8%) 的水平，因为大部分 trace 在 2048 tokens 内。\n      标准训练的 full_trace 用 standard loss 是 81.8%，但此处用 standard loss\n      所以结果基本一致。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Accuracy vs Trace Length\"\n        rows:\n          - length: \"VOTA (~80 tokens avg)\"\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            tokens_per_sample: 80\n          - length: \"256 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.862\n            tokens_per_sample: 256\n          - length: \"512 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.845\n            tokens_per_sample: 512\n          - length: \"1024 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.830\n            tokens_per_sample: 1024\n          - length: \"2048 tokens\"\n            accuracy: 0.820\n            tokens_per_sample: 2048\n          - length: \"Full trace (avg ~3200)\"\n            accuracy: 0.818\n            tokens_per_sample: 3200\n          - length: \"No trace\"\n            accuracy: 0.751\n            tokens_per_sample: 0\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Line plot: X 轴 = trace tokens (log scale: 0, 80, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 3200),\n        Y 轴 = accuracy。关键视觉特征：(1) VOTA 在 80 tokens 处达到最高点 99.2%，\n        与主曲线脱离（单独标注为 ★）；(2) 截断 trace 从 256→3200 呈微弱下降趋势\n        （86.2% → 81.8%），而非预期的上升；(3) no_trace 在 0 处为 75.1%。\n        标注：\"More trace ≠ better prediction — signal density dominates.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace length ablation 在 worst 档下产生 \"inverted U\" 或近似 monotonic decline：\n      短 trace 比长 trace 好（因为 error signal 的 density 更高），但都远不及 VOTA\n      （因为 VOTA 直接 isolate 了 signal）。这支持 \"information overload\" 叙事，\n      但在 worst 档解读下，\"overload\" 的本质不是 \"execution detail 干扰 reasoning\"\n      而是 \"keyword dilution 降低 pattern matching accuracy\"。\n      此图表在论文中仍有高价值——它直观展示了 signal density 假说，\n      只是 underlying mechanism 比原 framing 更 trivial。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Calibration analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"calibration_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      ECE (Expected Calibration Error) + reliability diagrams 对比\n      VOTA/no_trace/full_trace 的 calibration 质量。纯 eval 实验。\n    expected_results:\n      vota_ece: 0.008\n      vota_brier: 0.012\n      exception_only_ece: 0.015\n      exception_only_brier: 0.022\n      full_trace_ece: 0.085\n      full_trace_brier: 0.145\n      full_trace_label_only_ece: 0.068\n      full_trace_label_only_brier: 0.115\n      no_trace_ece: 0.165\n      no_trace_brier: 0.225\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，VOTA 和 exception_only 都有极低的 ECE，因为它们本质上是\n      near-deterministic 的 pattern matching（看到 ERROR → 高置信度 fail）。\n      calibration 好不是因为 \"深层理解产生了 well-calibrated uncertainty\"，\n      而是因为 signal 太强导致模型几乎不产生 uncertain predictions。\n      full_trace 的 ECE 较高反映了 noise-induced uncertainty，\n      no_trace 最高因为缺少 decision signal 导致系统性 miscalibration。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Calibration Metrics\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"VOTA\"\n            ece: 0.008\n            brier: 0.012\n            mean_confidence: 0.985\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            ece: 0.015\n            brier: 0.022\n            mean_confidence: 0.975\n          - condition: \"full_trace_label_only\"\n            ece: 0.068\n            brier: 0.115\n            mean_confidence: 0.890\n          - condition: \"full_trace\"\n            ece: 0.085\n            brier: 0.145\n            mean_confidence: 0.870\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            ece: 0.165\n            brier: 0.225\n            mean_confidence: 0.780\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        5-panel reliability diagram (one per condition)：X 轴 = predicted probability,\n        Y 轴 = observed frequency, 对角线 = perfect calibration。\n        VOTA 和 exception_only 的点集中在 (0,0) 和 (1,1) 两端（near-binary predictions），\n        几乎不在中间；no_trace 的点散布更广且偏离对角线。\n      - >\n        Single-panel ECE bar chart: 5 条件从低到高排列，VOTA/exception_only 几乎为零，\n        no_trace 最高。\n    analysis: >\n      Calibration 结果在 worst 档下的论文价值有限：VOTA 的 excellent calibration\n      是 near-perfect accuracy 的 trivial 后果，不提供额外 insight。\n      但 full_trace 的 poor calibration 可以用来支持 \"information overload causes\n      not just accuracy drop but also uncertainty increase\" 的叙事点。\n      建议放 Appendix 而非主文，避免 reviewer 指出 \"of course a 99% accurate\n      model is well-calibrated\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Seed robustness\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"seed_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      3 random seeds (42/123/456) 验证 VOTA 结果稳定性。McNemar test + bootstrap CI。\n    expected_results:\n      seed_42_accuracy: 0.992\n      seed_123_accuracy: 0.988\n      seed_456_accuracy: 0.990\n      mean_accuracy: 0.990\n      std_accuracy: 0.002\n      max_pairwise_gap: 0.004\n      mcnemar_max_pvalue: 0.55\n      bootstrap_ci_lower: 0.985\n      bootstrap_ci_upper: 0.995\n      n: 1190\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，VOTA 跨 seed 极其稳定（std < 0.2pp），因为 error flag signal\n      太强，training randomness 几乎不影响 learned decision boundary。任何 seed\n      都能在 early training 阶段学会 ERROR→fail 映射。高稳定性在论文中是正面结果\n      但在 worst 档叙事下也是 trivialness 的又一证据：真正困难的 task 不会有\n      0.2pp 的跨 seed 方差。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Seed Robustness (VOTA)\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: 42\n            accuracy: 0.992\n            pass_f1: 0.994\n            fail_f1: 0.986\n          - seed: 123\n            accuracy: 0.988\n            pass_f1: 0.992\n            fail_f1: 0.979\n          - seed: 456\n            accuracy: 0.990\n            pass_f1: 0.993\n            fail_f1: 0.982\n          - seed: \"Mean ± Std\"\n            accuracy: \"0.990 ± 0.002\"\n            pass_f1: \"0.993 ± 0.001\"\n            fail_f1: \"0.982 ± 0.004\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error bar plot: 3 seeds 的 accuracy ± CI，紧密聚集在 99% 附近。标注 'All pairwise McNemar p > 0.5'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Seed robustness 在所有 tiers 下都是正面的（结果稳定），区别在于解读。\n      在 worst 档下，需在 Discussion 中承认：\"The low variance across seeds\n      is consistent with our finding that the learned decision function is\n      dominated by a strong surface-level signal (error presence), which is\n      easily captured regardless of initialization.\" 但不需要 apologize——\n      robustness is robustness，reviewer 不会因为结果太稳定而 reject。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c7c66b2c-1925-497f-a2f7-83e1d0b40d81","total_cost_usd":0.41804024999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13895,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":12653,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13895,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12653,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13895},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8856,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008941,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12653,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13895,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.40909924999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f3874da5-258c-4496-a85f-bc848ac1bba0"}
